# FoodKnock line-ending policy.
#
# Detect text files automatically and keep LF as the normalized convention in
# Git's index, so CRLF/LF drift across Windows and other environments cannot
# recur. `eol=lf` sets the working-tree convention for files Git detects as
# text; this takes precedence over a developer's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# NOTE: this establishes the policy only. It does NOT rewrite existing files.
# Any one-time normalization of already-committed content should be done
# deliberately and separately (e.g. `git add --renormalize .` in its own
# commit), never as a side effect — see the audit report.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Confirmed binary assets — never apply text/EOL conversion ───────────────
# (SVG is intentionally omitted: it is XML text, not binary.)
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.webp  -text
*.gif   -text
*.ico   -text
*.pdf   -text
*.mp3   -text
*.mp4   -text
*.webm  -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text
*.otf   -text
*.eot   -text
